 "question": "What is sin(150°) and why?",
 "reference_answer": "sin 150° = 1/2. 150° (= 5π/6) lies in quadrant II; its point on the unit circle is (−√3/2, 1/2), and the sine is the y-coordinate, so sin 150° = 1/2. Its reference angle is 180° − 150° = 30°, so sin 150° = sin 30°; sine is positive above the x-axis (cos 150° = −√3/2).",
